    "result_text": "I added a default tax rate in Settings, and new invoices now start with it filled in. You can still change the rate on each invoice. `bin/e2e` builds and the acceptance spec passes (1/1).\n\nThe task mentioned an OfficeFloor server, but this app is plain Spring Boot (as CLAUDE.md says), so I wrote the server side the usual Spring way.\n\n**Database**\n- `V30__app_settings.sql` adds a one-row `app_settings` table holding `default_tax_pct`. It starts at 0 and only allows values from 0 to 100.\n\n**Server**\n- **Settings API:** a new `settings` package provides `GET` and `PUT /api/settings`. The `PUT` checks the value is between 0 and 100 with at most two decimal places.\n- **Invoice create:** the request now takes an optional `taxPct`. If it's left out, the server uses the default rate from Settings.\n- **Test reset:** `TestSupportController`'s reset now sets the default rate back to 0, so each test starts clean.\n\n**Front end**\n- **Settings page:** there's a new Settings page and nav link (`nav-settings`). It has the rate field (`settings-default-tax-rate`), a save button (`settings-save`), and save confirmation and error messages.\n- **Invoice form:** the new-invoice form on a job now has a tax rate field (`invoice-tax-rate`). It's filled from the default once settings load, unless you've already typed a rate, and the form returns to the default after each invoice is created.\n\nThings to know:\n- **What \"New invoice\" does:** the test needed an `invoice-new` button, but the add-invoice form is always visible. I didn't hide it behind the button, because that would break the existing `invoice-form-*` anchors. So the button clears the form back to the default rate and puts the cursor in the Amount field.\n- **Blank rate means no tax:** if you clear the rate field before adding an invoice, it's saved with 0% tax, not the default.\n- **Existing invoices don't change:** changing the setting only affects invoices created afterwards. You can still change a draft's rate on the invoice page as before.\n\nNo existing `data-testid` was renamed or removed.",
